# Librarian System unified development workspace

Local Git working base for package 0.3.71: LIBRA, HAYAKU, Flashback, LIA,
RETRACE, GRADIA and World Manager (WM). This checkout is a development source
repository, not an installable or qualified release package.

## Latest closeout checkpoint (2026-10-10)

Current repairs include LIBRA durable manifest reload/CAS and per-reference settlement,
HAYAKU approved-prefix preservation during passive edits and new capture/rejection,
WM fresh entity-shadow projection plus serialized, identity-bound removal,
Core3 shared-registry fallback consistency, and guarded cooperative typed-graph
node preparation. Typed graph checkpoints retain cancellation, policy-currentness,
exact graph parity and per-scope publication order.
The focused regression evidence is retained outside this repository. It does not
make the complete historical campaign a current-code pass.

The latest rebuilt Full/Min identity is checkpoint 245: all seven Full files match
source; seven Min files were generated and syntax-checked. WM Min is 4,468,250
bytes. Its build-size budget grew by 751 measured bytes from the retained
4,467,499-byte pre-entity-repair cap. This is artifact bookkeeping only.

Release qualification remains open. The retained synthetic 2,000-memory baseline
starved a 12-second readiness timer to about 149 seconds. Eventual completion
under a 600-second ceiling did not resolve that responsiveness defect. The new
typed-node checkpoints are a bounded mitigation; normalization and scope-index
preparation still require work and a final unchanged-workload responsiveness gate. Retained
active failures and the finite lower-tier reconciliation queue also remain open.
Actual Risu/Windows/model and updater lifecycle checks are unverified. Native
strong-authority/CAS support is not enabled or established by these tests.

Historical checkpoint details below remain dated records, not the current
qualification claim. Local development commits do not imply publication.

